data: {"id":"chatcmpl-e4738336-15c2-4978-b461-0b2dc7eeb6f4","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795545305,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"R23a and R23b (SAVEPOINT, ROLLBACK) are now considered correctly, based on position and offset values. The logic is now ensuring proper state restoration during rollback by focusing on the savepoint's offset and discarding any newer savepoints.\n- R23c (CHECKPOINT) and R23d (READ) don't have code, so nothing needs to change here. The readSet simply needs to include the key.\nResult construction will use an ordered, unmodifiable map for the state. Using `LinkedHashMap` ensures deterministic iteration, allowing for sorted keys. The unmodifiable map ensures safety.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-e4738336-15c2-4978-b461-0b2dc7eeb6f4","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795545305,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"`Map<>(state)` ensures the correct insertion order is retained, matching the deterministic requirements. The unmodifiable map guarantees read-only access, crucial for data integrity across all test operations, including `.get()`, `.entrySet()`, and `.equals()`. `Collections.unmodifiableMap` with `LinkedHashMap` provides fully deterministic iteration, regardless of external modifications.\n\nByte-to-char encoding:\nUsing `StandardCharsets.ISO_8859_1` (or `US_ASCII`) guarantees a direct 1:1 mapping of bytes to chars, where a char code equals the byte value. This resolves potential locale or charset inconsistencies.\n\nNow, let's look at edge cases. First, what if `log` length exceeds the 65536 limit?\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

